The problem statement contains a full solution sketch by Weisenberg embedded in the theorem's docstring: "It is clear that such a maximal $A$ must contain all non-squarefree numbers. It therefore suffices to find the largest size of a subset of all squarefree numbers in $\{1,\ldots,N\}$ such that any two have at least one prime factor in common. By the result of Chvátal [Ch74] discussed in [701] this is maximised by the set of all even squarefree numbers." Additionally, the Lean theorem statement `answer(True) ↔ ...` directly reveals that the answer is `True`.
